[#:seon.task{:name "close-turn-is-a-third-commit"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A replied run commits close-turn as a separate third transaction after settlement: a trivial root run costs 122-136 ms warm, about 75 ms of it three file-store commits (24-31 ms each), and close-turn is 32-36 ms. Fold the close into the settlement at the writer (hunk in the fix-write-cost landing), keeping the separate pass for issue-bearing agents and generated system turns."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/close-turn seon.turn/settle-batch!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/fix-write-cost-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-reload-between-forms-is-undetected"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A reload between the forms of one run, or between admission and settlement, is undetected; only a reload inside one evaluation is (call-detecting-program-change since e81cb51dc). Wrap the run's evaluate-and-settle in call-detecting-program-change with since captured at admission."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/call-detecting-program-change seon.turn/evaluate-sources}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/inv-lifecycle-storage-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/an-evaluation-that-overlaps-a-reload-is-not-detected.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-turn-pass-derives-its-work-twice"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Each agent pass derives next-agent-work on a fresh database value, runs the turn, then derives it again for the rewake (more-agent-work?); with episode-exhausted! (turns-left: episode-runs + max-episode-runs, four history queries) and opening-deferred? a trivial form spends ~12 ms and ~59 seon.db/q in turn derivations (2 ms for the same derivation on a held value). The rewake answer is decidable from the pass's own report (a closed run with no unanswered wake) without re-deriving from scratch; the budget reads scan the agent's whole turn history since assignment."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/step seon.turn/next-agent-work seon.turn/more-agent-work? seon.turn/turns-left}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/perf-eval-overhead-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-agent-form-is-read-again-by-each-consumer"
             :kind :function
             :intent "After the plan reads a reply, its source is read again by evaluable-source?, read-source, source-events (source-key and read-only-evaluation?, which also re-derives declarations with program/declaration-row), seon.sci.eval/one-event and install-row!'s test and deletion replays, besides the clj-kondo parse. A form is parsed once: carry the plan's events and the analyzed entities on the evaluation."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/evaluable-source? seon.sci.eval/one-event}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/eval-path-audit-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "receipt-attributes-are-a-hand-list"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.turn/receipt-terminal-attributes is a hand-written list of the receipt attributes the writer stores; it duplicates the receipt schema, so every new receipt key is silently dropped until someone edits the list (the LARGE VALUE cost keys of 2026-09-27 never landed because of it). Derive the stored attributes from the receipt's declared schema (CLAUDE.md: declare the partition on entity schemas, not in a hand list) and delete the list."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/receipt-terminal-attributes}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/large-value-feedback-opus-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-gate-exception-refuses-the-whole-run"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An exception inside the install gate escapes as a phase failure (turn.clj ~3551-3567), lands on ordinal 0 and leaves every other ordinal nil: the whole run is refused instead of its one form, violating the total REPL path. The failing form gets its diagnostic beside its value; the others keep theirs (probe-i, cc91a1e62). Worse: turn/phase (turn.clj:3551) catches only ExceptionInfo, so any other throwable (an NPE, fault 8f6fdfc0) escapes the turn step to Flow and the caller gets \"The awaited channel closed before completion\" with no value at all (fix-b, 5fffb1b48)."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/evaluate-sources}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/program-test-candidate-projection-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-nested-in-ns-loses-the-whole-run"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Probed on disposable branch p0-probe 2026-09-27: the run \"(do (in-ns 'p0.nested) 1) (+ 1 2)\" writes the second form's :seon.cluster.eval/ns as the lookup ref [:seon.ns/name p0.nested], but namespace-rows (turn.clj ~619) creates entities only for namespaces segmentation saw (top-level in-ns), so the settlement transaction is refused ('Nothing found for entity id', logged unbounded twice by Datahike) and the caller gets 'The awaited channel closed before completion' with no run id, no values, no events. Total-path violation. Every namespace an evaluation actually ran in or ended in is upserted as {:seon.ns/name sym} in the same settlement transaction (the owner's session-entity plan P2a, docs/research/agent-platform/repl-session-entity-design-2026-09-27.md problem 3)."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/evaluate-sources}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/repl-session-entity-design-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-refused-multi-form-settlement-returns-nothing"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The settlement of a refused multi-form run is recorded correctly (settle-batch-refusal! commits every receipt with its value, the refusal as its error and the fault), but seon.cluster.agent/evaluate-source! (agent.clj ~806-818) answers an opened run with only {:seon.turn/id :seon.db/db :seon.db/durable}, dropping :seon.turn.loop/refusal and the error outcome; direct callers get no error (the MCP bridge reads run-observation). Keep the refusal and outcome in the answer beside the run id (register-anywhere diagnosis db8937e8d)."
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/register-anywhere-diagnosis-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "schema-redeclaration-revalidates-unchanged-attributes"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Re-declaring an entity schema marks every one of its attributes affected (turn.clj ~1128-1133), so adoption re-validates all stored values of attributes whose declaration did not change; the work grows with history (a receipt re-declaration touches 43 attributes, 2,063 datoms, ~168K chars). Pass only attributes whose form changed; cost follows the change (fix-adoption-vector, bd3d35b19)."
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/register-anywhere-diagnosis-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-refused-refusal-settlement-throws-past-the-reply"
             :kind :function
             :intent "settle-batch-refusal! throws 'Batch refusal settlement was refused.' when its own write is refused (turn.clj ~4165); the pass rethrows through close-escaped-run! (turn.clj ~5728), turn-step's finally closes the reply, and evaluate-source! answers :seon.await/closed-error (agent.clj ~826). The caller sees 'awaited channel closed' while the fault (317111871b50, 3 occurrences 16:17-17:51Z 2026-09-27) goes only to root and to the agent's NEXT run. The nested in-ns trigger is fixed (9e61340b2); the throw path remains. Return both refusals as the value ({:refused-outcome :refusal-refused}) and answer them on the reply; boot recovery closes the run as for any failed terminal write. Related: a-refused-multi-form-settlement-returns-nothing (the non-throwing arm). Done when a regression whose refusal settlement is itself refused gets both refusals as data in its own reply, never a closed channel."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/settle-batch-refusal! seon.cluster.agent/evaluate-source!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/stability-sweep-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-transient-write-refusal-parks-the-agent-until-restart"
             :kind :function
             :intent "At 02:35Z 2026-09-27 memory pressure refused root's renderer three times; the write-refusal bound parked root's turn proc (fault c2268b2f) until the JVM died, and every submission was answered by closing its reply (turn.clj ~6044-6051; park recorded ~6155-6160). A park is left only by disarm/arm: right for a deterministic storm, wrong for a transient cause that clears. Neither fault was messaged (root is removed from its own recipients, error.clj ~1516-1520), and a parked root builds no next context. Keep wakes suppressed while parked, but give an explicit submission one attempt, answer its refusal on the reply, and clear the park on a committed write. Done when a regression that parks an agent through a transient refusal then submits after the cause clears gets an answered run, and a still-refused submission gets the park error on its reply."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/step seon.turn/write-refusal-bound seon.turn/record-write-refusal-fault!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/stability-sweep-2026-09-27.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/a-parked-turn-proc-pings-unknown-on-a-healthy-agent.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-definition-is-settled-twice"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A definition's facts are derived twice: once on the batch's working value, where the writer's validation admits them form by form (seon.turn.batch/apply-facts), then again at the writer on the head in the turn's one settlement (seon.turn.batch/program-facts-call, since S4a; before it, with-settled then receipt-settle-call's row-tx: x43 mean 315 ms and x93 mean 244 ms on pid 66629, the second on the writer thread where it serializes every write on the branch). Settle the working value's validated tx-data under an expected-basis fence (:datahike/expected-basis-t) and re-derive only when the head moved. Done when a defining form's facts are derived once (profile count per form) and a moved head still settles correctly."
             :must-read #{seon.turn.batch/program-facts-call seon.turn.batch/apply-facts seon.turn/settle-batch!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/perf-audit-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "row-tx-is-a-second-declaration-writer"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.turn/row-tx has no production caller since the fold writes declarations through seon.turn.batch/entity-facts and schema-tx (its concurrency check and schema attribute-change copy went in the writer-duplicates cut). Test fixtures in ten files still write declarations through it (datahike_fork, db, schema, schema_usage_guard, cluster/acquisition, program, sci/branch_execution, sci/eval, schema/datahike, schema/projection_writer). Done when those fixtures write through the fold's writer and row-tx with its declared-* helpers is deleted."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/row-tx seon.turn.batch/form-facts}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/one-repl-path-spec-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "eval-origin-has-no-producer-or-consumer"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent ":seon.eval/origin has no producer and no consumer (about fifteen turn.clj sites, e.g. turn.clj:116-117, 848) and Astra's seon.db/retention-check issue-authority code (db.clj:5470) is dead beside it. Done when both are deleted with their schema entries and callers converted in one commit."
             :must-read #{seon.db/retention-check}}
 #:seon.task{:name "turn-continue-read-results-arrive-before-done-takes-six-seconds"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "turn-continue read-results-arrive-before-done (:147) takes 5.8-7.3 s: undiagnosed. Done when a profile names the responsible armed functions and the test fits its bound."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/step}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-deep-value-loses-the-run"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An MCP sci run of (reduce (fn [v _] [v]) [] (range 10000)) on a branch agent (default pid 30874, 2026-10-07, waste-rank lane) evaluates in 34-47 ms, then its settlement is refused 'run transition refused: no-terminal-fact' (seon.turn/receipt-settle-call, validator :seon.turn/refused-error) and the reply carries only that 1,138-character diagnostic: the agent never receives its value (218-314 ms, 357-452 MB, 81-122 k armed calls, transact! x4). The one path is not total for deep values. Hypothesis to verify first: a recursive walk in recording or settlement (admission's project, the shown map or the receipt validation) overflows the stack and the throw becomes the refusal. Done when the case returns its value with a bounded shown text and settles as an ordinary evaluation; regression: that form through the one path, asserting the reply's value handle and the settled receipt."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/receipt-settle-call seon.sci.admit/admit seon.sci.eval/shown-result}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/waste-rank--large-values.edn" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/waste-rank--error-replies.txt"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "each-trivial-evaluation-retains-two-hundred-kilobytes"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Heap after System/gc grows linearly with ordinary evaluations: 100 MCP runs of (+ 1 2) on one branch agent grew default's live heap 2,562 -> 2,582 MB (~200 KB per run), and a further 100 runs added 22.9 MB in the live class histogram: Object[] +10.2 MB, datahike.datom.Datom +60,174 (about 600 per run for a 28-datom commit), persistent-sorted-set Leaf +6,296 and Branch +2,531 (default pid 30874, 2026-10-07, tmp/waste-rank/hist-diff-100-evals.txt). Retiring the branch did not release its heap within 3 s. Hypothesis: something keeps each commit's database value reachable (read evidence, a reply's basis, a world or cache key holding a db), pinning old index leaves. Find the holder with a heap dump's path to GC roots for the new Datoms and drop the reference at its producer (hold a commit id, never a db value). Done when 100 x (+ 1 2) leaves the live heap within noise (< 1 MB) and a retired branch's context and results are collectable; regression: the 100-run heap probe as a test with a declared memory bound."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/settle-batch! seon.batch/freeze-step seon.cluster.agent/release-context!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/waste-rank--hist-diff-100-evals.txt"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-deferred-wake-is-answered-by-silence",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "When `seon.turn/opening-deferred?` is true for a new wake, `next-agent-work` derives nil and nothing is recorded or delivered: the sender gets no reply, no fault, no diagnostic (agent r-turn-a, message ee63e682b520, default 2026-10-07). `episode-exhausted!` fires only on the pass that spends the last run, never for a wake arriving after. A wake the bound defers must reach the sender (or root) as data. Proof: a deftest that messages an exhausted agent and asserts the deferral is a stored, delivered error value.",
            :must-read
            #{seon.turn/next-agent-work seon.turn/episode-exhausted!},
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/plan-research/r-turn-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-message-from-root-never-refills-the-turn-bound",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "A message root sends an agent is an inside wake, so `seon.turn/outside-wake-t` stays 0 and `seon.turn/episode-runs` counts every turn the agent ever took. On default 2026-10-07, agent r-turn-a (branch :agent-cfd70b5547f7) with :seon.config.run/max-episode-runs 1 and one spent turn received root's message ee63e682b520 (seon.cluster.message/send! ... conn \"root\"): next-agent-work answered nil, outside-wake-t 0, spent 1, max 1, unanswered-wakes held the message. Root's work requests must refill the bound (or the bound must count calls per wake). Proof: a deftest where root messages an agent whose spent runs equal the dial and the agent takes one turn.",
            :must-read
            #{seon.turn/opening-deferred? seon.turn/outside-wake-t},
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/plan-research/r-turn-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-prose-only-reply-evaluates-its-first-word",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "When planned-sources finds no form (a prose-only model reply), the turn's freeze step plans the whole reply text as one row with no reader event, and read-row reads only that row's FIRST form as code: 'I will add two numbers.' evaluates the symbol I (Unable to resolve symbol) and the rest of the row is dropped unread; live run call 11 answered 'Invalid token: ##What' for its heading. The no-forms refusal ('Your reply had no form; only comments/prose. Send a form.') that planned-sources built never reaches the agent. Reproduce (default 722f110df): (seon.turn/planned-sources \"I will add two numbers.\" 'user 1048576) is the no-forms error; seon.turn/read-row over a row with that source reads I with end 1 of 23. Correct: the no-forms refusal is the row's read error, delivered once, and no prose is evaluated. Proof: a turn with a fixture reply of prose only answers the no-forms refusal as data.",
            :must-read #{seon.turn/read-row seon.turn/planned-sources},
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/plan-research/r-read-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-not-admitted-diagnostic-prints-its-write-attempt"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(defn h {:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :int] [:maybe :int]]} [x] x) through MCP answered a :diagnostics entry of about 980 tokens (default 2026-10-08): request id, producer digest, basis, three host frames and the whole refused transaction, while the rule broken sits only in the message, which a 40-token prefix from not-admitted lengthens until the printer cuts it mid-sentence. with-diagnostic prints the error whole (render.value/core-text [error]) instead of projecting it with seon.error/reply-value as evaluation errors are (seon.sci.eval/shown-failure). Done when the diagnostic is reply-value's map (type, message, offending) and an MCP regression bounds the reply at 150 tokens."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/with-diagnostic seon.turn/not-admitted seon.error/reply-value}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/agent-messages/messages-opus-messages.md"}}

 #:seon.task{:name "an-identical-re-record-conflicts-with-itself"
  :kind :function
  :intent "seon.cluster.evaluate-sources-test/ordered-evaluation-retains-one-explicit-basis-without-publication (red on HEAD 7a9ceb44a) transacts seon.turn/record-evaluated-tx's tx-data with its first element repeated, as the contract promises ('an identical cached identity is a no-op'); the writer answers {:seon.error/operation seon.turn/record-evaluated-call :seon.error/message \"run transition refused: recorded-content-conflict\"} and nothing is recorded (seven outcomes, zero receipts). Cause not isolated: the stored content (stored-record-content) differs from the expected content (recorded-evaluation) for the run's own just-written evaluations. Correct: find the key that differs and make saving and comparison read one projection. Done when that test is green."
  :must-read #{seon.turn/record-evaluated-call seon.turn/record-evaluated-tx}
  :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/review/red-triage.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-pass-reads-its-run-through-whole-branch-queries"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Every settlement runs seon.turn/terminal-agent-ordinal, a four-clause query whose plan fuse-scans every evaluation on the branch: 4.4-4.8 MB and 2.6-3.6 ms per pass on a branch of 742 evaluations, where the same answer from (d/entity run) and (d/datoms :avet :seon.cluster.eval/run run) costs 31 KB and 0.04 ms (defn-why, 2026-10-08). The other settlement queries (fault-window, spent-runs, opening-deferred?, system-run-plan, close-call, latest-answering-turn-t, next-ordinal, agent-dial) cost 0.5-2 MB each through the query floor (seon.db/a-datahike-query-walks-every-retained-result-bucket); together 14-16 MB of a 55 MB ordinary pass. Read a known entity's members by its identity (pull or AVET datoms), never by a query that joins the whole branch. Done when an ordinary pass's run bookkeeping allocates under 1 MB."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/terminal-agent-ordinal seon.turn/fault-window seon.turn/spent-runs seon.turn/opening-deferred?}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/defn-why/defn-why.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "turns-left-allocates-836-kilobytes-per-call"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.turn/turns-left (max-episode-runs plus episode-runs over the agent's runs) allocates about 836 KB per call (lane cs01a's report, 2026-10-08), and the current-state block calls it on every model call; what it must do is read one dial and count the agent's own runs in the current session. Done when one call's allocation follows the agent's session runs (measured with seon.pass-probe/window on parent and change), with a test asserting the count as data."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/turns-left seon.turn/episode-runs seon.turn/max-episode-runs}}

 #:seon.task{:name "the-test-step-results-never-reach-the-eval-reply"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.turn/step puts :seon.turn.loop/tests (the proofs' and the reaching tests' summaries, F4a/F4b) on the pass report, but seon.cluster.agent/evaluate-source! answers only select-keys of :seon.turn.loop/refusal and :seon.turn.loop/evaluated-sources, so the MCP eval_clj reply never shows a red proof or a red reaching test; the agent learns of it only by calling my.test/check or reading recorded results (observed in seon.cluster.turn-test/a-defn-breaking-a-reaching-test-shows-it-red-on-the-next-call, which can assert only the recorded result). Done when the summary reaches the reply as data and that test asserts :seon.turn.loop/reaching :seon.turn.loop/red from the reply."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/step seon.cluster.agent/evaluate-source!}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-executed-test-request-allocates-seven-hundred-megabytes-in-the-step"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Measured on default (2026-10-08, F4a running, seon.pass-probe/window as agent impl-f4b): an eval pass that evaluates a form costs 61-112 MB allocated and 85-120 ms with the proofs request answering from the record (seon.test/run 4-12 ms); the pass that changes code so a proof executes costs 865 MB and 586 ms (seon.test/run 440 ms, seon.test/select 76 ms), about 700 MB over the unchanged pass for one test world. Within the card's 400 ms interim for time, but the memory per executed request is the cost to bring down. Done when an executed one-test request allocates under 100 MB (seon.pass-probe/window on parent and change)."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run seon.test/select seon.turn/step}}

 #:seon.task{:name "two-branches-share-reach-declarations-is-red-beside-the-turn-tests"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.test-reaching-test/two-branches-of-one-program-share-reach-declarations is red when run in one JVM with seon.cluster.turn-test (check run d5281e6ec4d3, with F4b's automatic test step): seon.test.runner/retained-declarations answers nil for the parent (the 'derived once' and 'unrelated write keeps the key' assertions fail), and the test is green alone (check run 32238f76c1b8, 99 passes). Root hypothesis: cache eviction. The process cache is full (510 of 512 MB, 21 evictions of reach-related entries per the Opus landed review) and the step's test worlds add pressure, so the test asserts a retention that eviction legitimately drops. Proper fix: the base weighed correctly and held in the cluster's own registry (review finding #3), and the test not depending on cache retention. Filed here because seon.test.runner.edn is held by lane task-census; move it there. Done when the test is green whatever runs beside it, by the cause found."
             :must-read #{seon.test.runner/reach-declarations seon.test.runner/reach-revision-key}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-reply-shows-unreached-only-for-names-this-request-defined"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Root's step-noise finding, part 2 (part 1, dropping a run that executed nothing, landed with F4c as seon.turn/ran-something): `seon.turn/step` should show `:seon.test/unreached` only for the names the eval request itself defined that no test reaches, from the world member `:seon.batch/defined`, so a later pass never repeats it. Not done in F4c: the test summary carries no unreached key yet."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/step seon.turn/ran-something}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-bounded-step-that-leaves-queued-tests-wakes-nothing-when-no-member-ran"
             :kind :function
             :intent "F4c: `seon.turn/continue-queue` rewakes the agent only when the continuation ran at least one queued test; with the dial below the selection cost no member ever starts and the queue waits for the next wake. Unreached by a default 10 s dial; named so a smaller dial is understood."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/step seon.turn/continue-queue}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-red-proof-carries-no-reason"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A red test's reason is invisible (PB-15 dogfood run, lane dogfood-pb15, default, 2026-10-08): the test step's :red names only the test; :seon.render.test/failures carries only the symbol; \"exceeded 5000 ms\" and \"Worker-global state changed\" each needed manual digs (three in all); result entries lack :seon.test/passed?, so (remove :seon.test/passed?) matched every entry. Done when each red in the step summary and in the my.test/check failure render carries its failure data (test, expected/actual, or the bound or drift reason) and every result entry has :seon.test/passed?, with a regression on a red by bound and a red by drift."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/step seon.render.test/render-ai seon.test/recorded-result}}
 #:seon.task{:name "ai-attempt-stores-printed-copies-of-settings-and-usage"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Evidence for ledger row SR-G: :seon.ai.attempt/settings-edn is written as (pr-str settings) in seon.turn (and usage-edn likewise), a stored printed copy and a second printer. Store the settings and usage as data, or only their digest and ids."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/step}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-model-pass-never-sees-its-test-step"
             :kind :function
             :intent "After a model pass that evaluated a form, `seon.turn/step` runs the proofs and reaching tests but offers the summary only on an MCP reply channel; the model's next prompt carries neither the summary nor the current-state block, so the model never learns its proof is still red (live-agent run, agent live-flash, default 6cc5dbbb4, 2026-10-08: nine passes, the agent learned the proof's status only by evaluating (seon.context/current-state) itself). Covered by the block-last assembly (ledger CS-03a) once it lands; done when a model pass's next prompt shows the proofs' status that pass's step recorded."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/step seon.context/model-context}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-stop-during-model-context-assembly-records-errors"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An orderly disarm while a model pass is assembling its context (seon.context/model-context inside the call turn's phase) interrupts the pass but records two error occurrences; a stop's wrapped interrupt is no error. Before CX-1 the test's stand-in redefined seon.cluster.prompt/prompt, which the pass no longer called, so the test hung instead (lane rip-context, 2026-10-08). Done when the interrupted pass closes as interrupted with no error recorded."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/call-turn seon.context/model-context seon.cluster.agent/disarm!}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-throwing-test-step-loses-its-cause"
             :kind :function
             :intent "When the automatic test step throws a non-refusal (a NullPointerException inside seon.test/changes while lane test-step worked, 2026-10-09), seon.turn/test-step answers only {:seon.error/message \"The automatic test step threw; the pass's values stand.\" :seon.error/exception-class \"java.lang.NullPointerException\"}: no cause chain, no throw site, so the agent and root cannot tell which owner failed without a debug build. A deliberate translation keeps the cause. Done when the step's error carries the cause chain (`:seon.error/chain`) of the thrown exception and a reply test asserts it names the throwing function."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/test-step seon.error.refusal/diagnostic}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-root-request-runs-the-clusters-whole-drift-as-reaching-tests"
             :kind :function
             :intent "On default at e040662e4 (lane platform-route, 2026-10-09), a root SCI eval_clj request whose one form was refused by its contract (`(my.agent/retire-branch! {:seon.agent/id ...})`) ran a test step of 10,324 ms of a 10,415 ms request: 3 red, 1 errored and about 1,600 tests left pending, selected by `seon.test/changes` over the cluster branch's whole difference from its published commit. The next root request gave no answer within the bridge's 32 s and runtime_status then showed `seon.sci.kernel/acquire-arm` refusing evaluations for memory pressure (5 occurrences, heap live 1.79 GB of 4 GB). Done when a root request's test step costs what its own forms changed (`seon.turn/test-step` selecting through `seon.test/changes`), not the cluster's drift from its base."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/test-step seon.test/changes seon.sci.kernel/memory-pressure}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-read-only-request-re-runs-the-branchs-reaching-tests"
             :kind :function
             :intent "After an agent branch redefines `seon.task/candidate-dangling` and its tagged deftest in `seon.task-ingestion-test` (both green), later eval requests that define nothing re-execute the reaching tests: lane merge-path on default a6cbe4fcf, 2026-10-10, `(let [d (seon.db/db)] ...)` and `(my.test/check {...})` replies each carried `:seon.cost/tests` count 2, 755-1,403 ms and 1.7 GB allocated, a test step of 1.4-2.7 s per reply. Another branch's read-only `(my.program/propose-merge! {})` ran no test (test step 29 ms), so reuse holds sometimes; which reuse condition fails is not measured. AGENTS.md: unchanged results are answered from their record. `seon.turn/test-step` selects the branch's whole difference from its base through `seon.test/changes` each request (the root form of this class is `seon.turn/a-root-request-runs-the-clusters-whole-drift-as-reaching-tests`). Done when a request that changes no declaration executes no test and answers its reaching tests from their record (`:seon.test/unchanged`), with a `seon.profile/measure` regression on the step's cost."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/test-step seon.turn/run-reaching seon.test/changes seon.test/select}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-wake-reopens-a-finished-task"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.turn/next-agent-work` opens a turn for any unanswered wake, so an agent whose task is done, capped or given back is reopened by the next message: root's questions to chain2-forgive-2 became 11 more calls of task work (DYNAMIC-CONTEXT stage 2). Done when the end of a model agent's task (`seon.turn/task-end`) asserts `:seon.agent/admission-closed-tx` once (`seon.turn/end-task-call`) and no later wake opens a turn for it."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/next-agent-work seon.turn/task-end seon.turn/end-task-call seon.context/task-done?}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/schedule/cards/DYNAMIC-CONTEXT.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-task-end-never-reaches-root"
             :kind :function
             :intent "When a model agent's task ends nobody is told, and a green task proposes no merge: the turn loop stops calling the model once the proofs are green, so `my.program/propose-merge!` never runs and root's `my.program/prepare-merge!` has nothing to take (plan §0, chain run 4 gap 1; DYNAMIC-CONTEXT stage 3). Done when every task end (`seon.turn/task-end`) sends root exactly one message holding references only (`:seon.task/end`, the task's id as `:seon.message/about`) and, ended green, the agent's own proposal (`my.program/proposal!`) named by `:seon.task/merge`, which `my.program/prepare-merge!` takes."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/task-end seon.turn/end-task-call my.program/proposal! my.program/propose-merge! my.program/prepare-merge! seon.cluster.message/send!}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/schedule/cards/DYNAMIC-CONTEXT.md" "docs/seon/plan.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-reached-red-test-keeps-a-task-from-ending-done"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.turn/task-end` answers `:done` only when the task's proofs are green and no test the agent's change reaches is red on its branch (`seon.context/task-done?`, read from the results the turn's test step records there, `seon.test.runner/latest-results`). With proofs green and a reached test red, the loop continues and the next context shows the red test; at the cap the end is `:capped`. Loop round 2 (2026-10-10): agent r2-cost-diff (branch :agent-188875ebeb62, task `seon.batch/an-unchanged-interpreted-definition-shows-no-cost-entry`) ended `:done` and proposed merge task 3ea28f83185c the moment its proof went green; the merge gate refused it (run 5649676309ec) with three reaching tests red in seon.request-cost-test, against AGENTS.md: an agent requests a merge only after no test its change broke is red on its source branch."
             :must-read #{seon.turn/task-end seon.context/task-done? seon.turn/next-agent-work seon.test.runner/latest-results}}]
